Generate comprehensive metadata for a data widget including title, description, category, and subcategory based on the provided data.

METADATA REQUIREMENTS:

TITLE:
- Create a concise, descriptive widget title (3-6 words)
- Should clearly indicate what the data represents
- Use financial/business terminology when appropriate
- If the data, description, filename, or metadata contains material identifiers such as a ticker/company and an explicit reporting period, include those identifiers in the title when it remains concise. Preserve visible year text from the source, and do not drop quarter, fiscal year, or date information when it distinguishes the dataset.
- Examples: "Stock Price Tracker", "Revenue Performance", "Market Volatility"

DESCRIPTION:
- Start directly with the data type/category (e.g., "Financial performance metrics", "Stock price movements", "Revenue breakdown")
- Do NOT use introductory phrases like "This table presents", "This data shows", "Analysis of", etc.
- Be specific about the domain (financial, operational, statistical, etc.)
- Include relevant time periods, sectors, or categories if evident
- Keep to one factual sentence

CATEGORY:
- High-level classification of the data domain
- Common categories: "Equity", "Economy", "Crypto", "Fixed Income", "Derivatives", "Alternative", "ESG", "Sports", "Prediction Markets", "Custom"
- Choose the most appropriate category based on data content

SUBCATEGORY:
- More specific classification within the category
- Examples for Equity: "Fundamentals", "Technical", "Options", "Screening", "Performance"
- Examples for Economy: "GDP", "Inflation", "Employment", "Trade", "Indicators"
- Examples for Crypto: "Prices", "Market Cap", "Trading", "DeFi", "NFT"
- Examples for Sports: "Racing", "Football", "Basketball", "Tennis", "Olympics"
- Examples for Prediction Markets: "Politics", "Sports", "Technology", "Economics", "Entertainment"

ANALYSIS GUIDELINES:
- Analyze ONLY the provided data - no creative content
- For tables: identify data type from headers/columns (financial ratios, stock prices, performance metrics, betting markets, etc.)
- For time series: note temporal patterns and data categories
- For prediction/betting markets: identify the event type and market structure
- Use ticker symbols, financial terms, sports terminology, or domain identifiers when present
- Leverage metadata, filenames, and indices for context

