EXAMPLES:

Example 1 - Stock Data:
Title: Apple Stock Analysis
Description: Daily stock price movements and technical indicators for AAPL equity.
Category: Equity
Subcategory: Technical

Example 2 - Economic Data:
Title: GDP Growth Tracker
Description: Quarterly gross domestic product growth rates across major economies.
Category: Economy
Subcategory: GDP

Example 3 - Options Data:
Title: Options Flow Monitor
Description: Real-time options trading volume and open interest for S&P 500 components.
Category: Equity
Subcategory: Options

Example 4 - Sports Betting Data (No Parameters):
Title: F1 Race Predictions
Description: Formula 1 Azerbaijan Grand Prix winner and constructor betting markets with Yes/No outcomes.
Category: Sports
Subcategory: Racing

Example 5 - Parametrized Event Search:
Title: Event Search
Description: Sports betting market search results with event details, timelines, and betting options.
Category: Sports
Subcategory: Racing
(Note: Generic title works for F1, politics, entertainment, etc.)

Example 6 - Parametrized Market Details:
Title: Market Details
Description: Prediction market event information including status, timeline, and available betting markets.
Category: Prediction Markets
Subcategory: Sports
(Note: Generic enough to work for any market type)

Example 7 - SQL Query (Simple Select):
Title: User Account Data
Description: User account information including profile details and account status.
Category: Custom
Subcategory: Database

Example 8 - SQL Query (Aggregation):
Title: Monthly Revenue Summary
Description: Aggregated sales revenue grouped by month with product category breakdown.
Category: Custom
Subcategory: Database

Example 9 - SQL Query (Join):
Title: Order Customer Details
Description: Order records with associated customer information and shipping addresses.
Category: Custom
Subcategory: Database

Example 10 - SQL Query (SEC Filing with ITEM_TITLE filter):
Title: MD&A Disclosure Content
Description: Management's Discussion and Analysis narrative text extracted from SEC 10-K and 10-Q filings.
Category: Equity
Subcategory: Fundamentals
(Note: The ITEM_TITLE filter specifies this is MD&A content, not generic "KPIs" based on the table name)

Example 11 - Python Query (Dataframe Aggregation):
Title: Revenue Trend Analysis
Description: Python dataframe analysis calculating revenue trends and summary metrics across reporting periods.
Category: Equity
Subcategory: Fundamentals

Example 12 - Python Query (Chart Preparation):
Title: Volatility Comparison Prep
Description: Python workflow transforming market data into comparative volatility metrics for charting and analysis.
Category: Equity
Subcategory: Technical

Output format:
Title: [Short descriptive widget title]
Description: [Direct, factual sentence about data type/nature - no introductory phrases]
Category: [High-level data domain category]
Subcategory: [Specific classification within category]

Remember: Be precise and domain-specific. Use standard financial/business terminology.
